Upstream commit the port matches:
  0ac649541fca5b7a80bb724a308229fa4cfb2574   2026-11-09T22:18:40+01:00

How to port forward: diff the upstream files below against that commit (git diff 0ac6495..HEAD -- dll/ai/<file>)
and carry the changed decisions into the Lua module named. The port keeps the decisions (budgets, targets, timings,
the force's rules), not the engine patches: what upstream patches into the original exe (danger routes, honest
vision, the group move, the unload retries) is a C++ helper of this engine (docs/AI_LUA_UNITS.md §4, §11).

Per-file map (upstream dll/ai/<file> -> this folder). Each line says PORTED, PARTLY (what is missing), ENGINE (a
C++ helper of this engine stands in, nothing to port) or NOT STARTED.

  econ.c        PARTLY -> econ.lua (budget, workers, epoch), army.lua (choice). Ported: budget_reserve /
                spend_reserve (the epoch reserve; from farms only what the income cannot bring back),
                hook_add_resource (the military account and its income shares), econ_targets (the worker plan by
                shortfall and rate), gather_research, early_requirements, the copper plan's epoch attempt,
                substitute_soldier (the strongest affordable soldier), hoard caps. Missing: citizens_home (the
                engine's finders keep citizens on safe sites), train_budget's priority rows (priority.c).
  early.c       PARTLY -> econ.lua (towers), tactics.lua (bait). Ported: early_towers (two towers by the town
                centre: the front and the citizens' side), the builders, tower_bait (the citizens hit lead the
                raiders under the towers, epochs 1-2). Missing: early_militia (the engine's reflexes, ai.reflex,
                stand in).
  food.c        PORTED -> econ.lua (workers, claims): food_plan_needs (the citizens' food, the real wood need), the
                hunters, the patches (the engine's claims stand in for the site lists).
  mines.c       PORTED -> econ.lua (settlements): mine_drops / wood_drops (a settlement at the unworked mine or
                forest edge nearest a drop site).
  citizens.c    PORTED -> econ.lua (citizens): cz_targets (the citizens wanted from the mines' places, FEED).
  defence.c     PARTLY -> econ.lua (towers), army.lua (home guard, muster, hold the town), tactics.lua (bunkers).
                Ported: def_refresh (the fronts: towards the nearest enemy buildings known), defence_tick (towers at
                the fronts and the outposts), home_guard, muster. Missing: WALLS (the 11-tile straight wall 3 tiles
                before two towers at a front, the gate in its middle), ENCLOSE (the octagon round the town, the
                coast's ring on an island), DOCK POCKETS; the engine has ai.wall / ai.gate / ai.lock for them.
  armies.c      PARTLY -> army.lua: the force (one land army ordered as one: home at the station, the push at the
                attack time when it beats the enemy at the target by AR_GO_PCT, the judge every AR_JUDGE_EVERY, home
                under AR_BACK_PCT twice running, the next building, the raid answered, the way home as a convoy).
                Missing: the detachments (the raid parties on the enemy's economy and outposts).
  stage.c       PORTED -> army.lua: the staging point (the last point of the way out of the enemy's reach).
  intel.c       ENGINE -> C++ (ai.memory, ai.seen): honest vision's memory (buildings until seen gone, soldiers
                remembered 3 minutes).
  danger.c      ENGINE -> C++ ai.danger "threat": the threat map (defences at range, soldiers, hurt citizens).
  cover.c       ENGINE -> C++ ai.danger "lost": DANGER_LOST (where own units traded badly, 20 minutes).
  shiproute.c   ENGINE -> C++ ai.route (cells): danger-aware routes.
  army.c        PORTED -> econ.lua (buildings): army_plan BUILD (one more production building of the kind trained
                when the producers are busy).
  attack.c      PARTLY -> tactics.lua (siege), C++ ai.route (the routing round known defences). Ported: the siege
                controller (siege_want / siege_train: 2 + a quarter of the known defences, at most 4, from a Siege
                Factory, a pause after 3 lost in 10 minutes), site_danger (the engine's blocked == "tower").
                Missing: the weak spots (the target's least defended side), the breaches (through a known wall away
                from the towers), the commander's patches (the engine's attack groups are not used: the force is
                the port's).
  garrison.c    PORTED -> tactics.lua (garrison): the settlement upgrades (spare citizens into the drop site with
                the most metal mines near).
  counterfire.c PORTED -> tactics.lua (counterfire): the shooters out of reach answered by the soldiers near when
                they win by 1.5 (the micro step, 250 ms for upstream's 2 s).
  bunker.c      PARTLY -> tactics.lua (bunkers, shelter): a Fortress by the drop site nearest the base once
                citizens were hurt three times in two minutes, the citizens hit shelter in it, let out when quiet.
                Missing: the shelf (the fortress's own soldiers), bk_capacity's airport part.
  navy.c        PARTLY -> navy.lua, lib/navy.lua. Ported: the sea scout (a warship looks over the water from the
                Stone Age), the navy account's share, transports and a warship from the account. Missing: the
                fishing boat type, docks and fleet room (stage 1), the warship mix (navy_pick, stage 2).
  fleet.c       NOT STARTED (the fleet led as one: massing under the towers while weaker, the strike once stronger,
                the split when clearly stronger, the fishing boats guarded). lib/navy.lua's N.fleet_step is the
                engine-side move helper only.
  transports.c  ENGINE -> C++ (the unload retries at the next shore tile; the stalled transport watchdog is the
                engine's own transport goal). Nothing to port.
  landing.c     PARTLY -> navy.lua (landing), lib/navy.lua (N.beach, N.plan, N.landing_step). Ported: the beach
                (the weakest defended shore of the target's continent), the size (1.2 x of 1.4 x the beach's
                strength), board / sail / unload with retries. Missing: the bridgehead (citizens, towers), the
                landing's own fleet escort, the second wave, the return of the transports.
  expand.c      NOT STARTED (expansion to other islands: the empty continent with the most mines nearest the
                base, the mining camp with a drop site, towers and a barracks, the outpost ferries).
  towns.c       PARTLY -> econ.lua (settlements: a town centre instead of a settlement at a far mineral site from
                the Copper Age). Missing: RESOURCE TOWNS (the richest free mine group 32-90 tiles out, its
                towers_per_town towers, production), FORWARD BASES (the tactical operations centre near the enemy),
                the towns' defences and walls.
  airstrike.c   NOT STARTED (the bombers held as a wing of AF_WING, trained while a position needs them, the
                bombing run on the shooters' spot).
  diplo.c       NOT STARTED (answer war, the blocks, the vassals, the tributes; the engine has ai.diplomacy and
                ai.tribute for them; the human chat lines and peace offers through the diplomacy screen are not in
                this engine's AI path).
  spoils.c      NOT STARTED (a resigned player's units roam and its buildings change hands: an engine behaviour of
                the player out of the game, to be weighed against this engine's defeat rule).
  skirmish.c    NOT STARTED (the sharpshooters' sorties on a position that holds the force's way).
  metal.c       NOT STARTED (best_per_metal: the soldier that does most per gold + iron against the enemy's army;
                surplus_cheap; workers_to_metals; fleet_by_enemy).
  mass.c        NOT STARTED (the army as one: reinforcements gather under cover and join as groups, never a
                trickle).
  fronts.c      NOT STARTED (the border cells: where its land meets land the enemy can walk over; the front armies).
  sites.c       ENGINE -> C++: the next engine's finders take the mine nearest a drop site, the bush nearest a drop
                site, refuse a site behind known towers (the site's blocked == "tower"). Nothing to port.
  packing.c     NOT STARTED (tight_build: production buildings placed touching their kind without cutting a way;
                upstream default 0).
  priority.c    NOT STARTED (the priority list: one row for each thing the AI saves for, every spender asks it).
  forces.c      PARTLY -> C++ ai.reach (the continents), army.lua (the enemy army in its territory as the threat).
                Missing: enemy_objective (an objective building of the target), the walk-and-fight record.
  stats.c       NOT STARTED (fight_estimate: st_ratio from the game's damage tables; upstream default 0, the
                summed hit points x attack of ai.strength stand in).
  settings.c    PORTED -> settings.lua: the [ai_base] defaults of config/ageofai.ini at that commit.

